From: Geodesic Research <noreply@geodesicresearch.org>
Date: Sun, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: normalize allgather dispatcher output by EP size

Regenerated 2026-07-27 against pin fa774820 (upstream 6cd6ea530 + nvrx carry).
The original patch's second hunk (a cosmetic blank-line change in the alltoall
dispatcher) no longer applies after the shared-experts overlap rework and was
DROPPED — only this substantive hunk remains. Upstream still has no equivalent
fix: MoEAllGatherTokenDispatcher.combine_preprocess returns un-normalized
output at the new pin. The patch remains deliberately NOT auto-applied
(nothing selects the allgather dispatcher — every config forces alltoall).

---
diff --git a/megatron/core/transformer/moe/token_dispatcher.py b/megatron/core/transformer/moe/token_dispatcher.py
index 4c4b65679..24fb5bd8e 100644
--- a/megatron/core/transformer/moe/token_dispatcher.py
+++ b/megatron/core/transformer/moe/token_dispatcher.py
@@ -334,6 +334,13 @@ class MoEAllGatherTokenDispatcher(MoETokenDispatcher):
             routing_map=self.local_map,
             fused=self.config.moe_permute_fusion,
         )
+        # Normalize by EP size to compensate for gradient inflation from AllGather.
+        # AllGather duplicates tokens across EP ranks, so each rank's expert outputs
+        # contribute to gradients independently. ReduceScatter sums these contributions,
+        # inflating gradients by ep_size. Dividing here keeps gradient magnitudes
+        # consistent with the AlltoAll dispatcher.
+        if self.ep_size > 1:
+            unpermuted_local_hidden = unpermuted_local_hidden / self.ep_size
         return unpermuted_local_hidden
 
     def token_combine(self, hidden_states):
